---
description: Avoid brittle UI presence tests; assert behavior and outcomes instead
globs: tests/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI and feature test assertions

Do **not** add tests whose main assertion is that markup, copy, or CSS exists unless that encodes a real requirement.

## Do not test

- Tailwind/CSS classes (`font-display`, `px-4`, `fixed top-0`, `badge-error`, `bg-secondary`)
- Layout/spacing implementation details
- Exact image dimensions, `srcset` breakpoints, or footer/wrapper markup
- Every `data-ui` hook on a page when one outcome check suffices
- Label/copy presence when the same behavior is already covered by service/unit tests
- `novalidate`, Alpine/JS implementation strings, or other HTML plumbing

```php
// BAD — breaks on harmless styling refactors
$response->assertSee('font-display', false);
$response->assertSee('fixed inset-0 z-0', false);
$this->assertStringContainsString('sm:px-6', $html);

// BAD — duplicates UpcomingFeedQueryService tests
->assertSee(__('ui.dashboard.stats_interested_activities'))
->assertSeeHtml('data-ui="dashboard-stat-interested-activities"');
```

## Do test

- **Authorization and conditional UI** — who sees create links, tabs, admin actions
- **User-visible outcomes** — filtered listing names, stat counts, modal content, redirects, DB changes
- **Integration wiring** — preview opens modal, form errors appear, tab switches on validation failure
- **Stable behavioral contracts** — preview button vs navigate link, enrollment badge when window is open

Prefer asserting **state and outcomes**:

```php
// GOOD — behavior through view data
->assertViewHas('upcomingInterestedActivitiesCount', 1)
->assertSeeHtml('data-ui="dashboard-activity-stats"');

// GOOD — permission rule
->assertDontSee(__('ui.nav.create_event'), false)
->assertSee(route('activities.create'), false);

// GOOD — end-to-end filter result
->assertSee('Free Places Open Activity')
->assertDontSee('Free Places Full Activity');
```

## Layering

- Put counting, filtering, sorting, and authorization logic in **unit/service tests**.
- Use feature/Livewire tests as a thin smoke layer: one check that UI reflects the seeded outcome.
- Do not duplicate both layers with label enumeration and count logic.

## When removing UI

If a test fails because a feature was intentionally removed, update or delete the test. Do not add new presence tests to replace removed ones unless the requirement still exists.
